From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] SCSP: sleep instead of spinning while waiting for the SH2

The asynchronous SCSP thread waited for SH2 time by reading the M68K
counter in a tight loop: 70 % of its samples (ScspAsynMainCpuTime +
getM68KCounter), a whole Cortex-A53 core kept busy for the whole game.
After 64 reads without progress it now sleeps 50 us: the sound runs at
most that far behind the SH2, and SyncCPUtoSCSP still waits for the
frame. Virtua Fighter 2 fight: SCSP thread 97 -> 32 % of a core, about
0.4 fps fewer (28.6 -> 28.2, within the run-to-run spread).

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/yabause/src/scsp.c
+++ b/yabause/src/scsp.c
@@ -5527,10 +5527,18 @@
     u64 m68k_done_counter = 0;
     u64 m68k_integer_part = 0;
     u64 m68k_cycle = 0;
+    /* nuubOS: wait for SH2 time without spinning a whole core. The
+     * loop read the counter the SH2 thread writes as fast as it could
+     * (70 % of this thread); after a short spin it sleeps 50 us: the
+     * sound runs at most that far behind the SH2, and SyncCPUtoSCSP
+     * still waits for the frame. */
+    int idle = 0;
     do {
       m68k_integer_part = getM68KCounter() >> SCSP_FRACTIONAL_BITS;
       m68k_cycle = m68k_integer_part - pre_m68k_cycle;
       if (thread_running == 0) break;
+      if (m68k_cycle == 0 && ++idle >= 64)
+        YabThreadUSleep(50);
     } while (m68k_cycle == 0);
 
     m68k_inc += m68k_cycle;
